			"notes": "## Highlights\n\nSecond release with **major fixes on multi-POV merging**.\n\n### Critical fixes\n\n- **Missing chunks fixed** — `PlayerRespawnS2CPacket` and `GameJoinS2CPacket` now primary-only (EGO). Previously, secondary sources were dragging the client into their dimension, silently dropping primary chunks.\n- **Entity dedup re-enabled** with runtime registry access via `DynamicRegistryManager.ImmutableImpl(Registries.ENTITY_TYPE)`. No more duplicate zombies/items.\n- **Secondary POV always visible** — synthesized `PlayerInfoUpdate(ADD_PLAYER)` + `AddEntity(PLAYER)` for each secondary source. Their position tracks via `accurate_player_position` → `TeleportEntity` translation.\n- **WORLD LWW re-enabled** — `BlockUpdate`/`SectionBlocksUpdate` now go through `WorldStateMerger` for last-write-wins arbitration. No more block flickers.\n\n### Other improvements\n\n- Per-replay checkbox UI (replaces global toggle)\n- Rich snapshots in every `cN.flashback` segment (fixes empty world after seek)\n- Merge output split every 6000 ticks (avoids 2GB Java array limit)\n- Primary source = the one starting first (cleaner timeline opening)\n- `FORGET_LEVEL_CHUNK` + `REMOVE_ENTITIES` primary-only (less flickering)\n- Markers aggregated from all sources\n- `SET_CHUNK_CACHE_CENTER` / `_RADIUS` / `SIMULATION_DISTANCE` classified EGO\n- Flashback `accurate_player_position_optional` routed to LOCAL_PLAYER (primary-only)\n- Progress bar with percentage + phase text\n- Auto-refresh replay list after merge\n- Shorter merge output names: `merged_<timestamp>.zip`\n\n### Known limitations (still)\n\n- 4+ POV merge: works, with occasional visual imperfections in areas covered by multiple POVs.\n- Multiple dimensions: camera follows primary only. Secondary POVs in a different dimension appear at wrong coords.\n\n### Tests: 127 green\n\nFull CHANGELOG: https://github.com/Zeffut/MultiView/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md"
		},
